      }
    ],
    "summary": "I couldn't put five drawers in one base. A drawer can only go on the cut face of a half base, and a half base has just one cut face, so it holds one drawer. A full base holds none. I swapped the full base for a north half base and fitted the one drawer it allows. After that, the configurator offered no more drawer spots. The only way to get more is to add cells next to or on top of the base, and you asked for nothing beside or on it. I left out the end caps and joint bolts my usual finishing steps would add, so nothing else is fitted to the base. The check came back with no errors and no part collisions.",
